Description: Pimax Crystal Super / Dream Air VR hub for Linux
 PiBridge is a one-app, one-click VR hub for Pimax headsets (Crystal Super and
 Dream Air) on Linux: a Qt 6 desktop app plus the engine binaries for inside-out
 6DoF/SLAM tracking, eye tracking, controller tracking, room setup, video
 recording and a VR home.
 .
 The package bundles the PiBridge Monado SteamVR driver (used as a SteamVR driver;
 the standalone monado-service is not shipped) and the ONNX Runtime it needs,
 which are not available as distribution packages. OpenCV, the Vulkan loader,
 Qt 6, ffmpeg and every other library are used from their system packages.
 .
 SteamVR is the runtime (Recommends: steam); the per-user setup (enabling the
 user services and registering the SteamVR driver) is done by the app on first
 run. The optional inside-out (Pimax-engine) path needs winbridge, which is
 shipped as source and built with the pibridge-build-winbridge helper
 (Suggests: wine, mingw-w64).
